id: pm-2sbj8p
title: "ADR: convergence model for concurrent workspaces — field-level merge semantics versus conflict-free replicated state at thousands of agents"
description: ""
type: Decision
status: open
priority: 2
tags[8]: adr,concurrency,decision,federation,long-term,merge,multi-agent,storage
created_at: "2026-07-24T23:48:31.411Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-24T23:48:31.411Z"
author: maintainer-agent
estimated_minutes: 900
acceptance_criteria: "The decision states the concurrency and divergence regime under which field-aware three-way merge is proven sufficient, with measured evidence; Rejected alternatives are recorded with their reasons, including full conflict-free replicated data types and operation-log-only storage; Any adopted change states its format_version and migration implications and its effect on the plain-text, git-diffable storage property; The decision names the acceptance evidence source — the merge conformance suite and the simulation harness — rather than asserting a position"
goal: provable-history
objective: "Decide, with evidence, whether field-aware three-way merge is sufficient at the stated concurrency target or whether convergent replicated state is required"
value: The shipped merge drivers resolve conflicts correctly for the concurrency levels observed so far. Whether they still do at thousands of simultaneous agents across many branches is an open question that silently constrains the federation and scale milestones.
impact: Determines the storage format's long-term shape. Adopting convergent replicated state later is a format migration; adopting it never is a ceiling on concurrency. Both are expensive to discover by accident.
outcome: "A recorded decision with the rejected alternatives, the evidence that decided it, and the format_version implications stated explicitly."
why_now: The merge-safety program has closed and federation is on the roadmap. The decision is cheapest before the GA contract freezes the storage format policy and while a simulation harness can still generate the evidence.
parent: pm-m2u1
risk: high
confidence: low
